UAS-CPE is a Physics-Secure Engine (PSE) integrating GRMHD, symplectic Hamiltonian mechanics, post-quantum cryptography, and zero-knowledge verification. Phase-space states are projected onto $T^*M$ and evolved on an 8-level AMR hierarchy. Invariants are enforced via hardware feedback. Execution states are encapsulated via ML-KEM-1024, evaluated over CKKS SIMD ciphertexts, and proven via Halo2/Plonky3. Epoch states are committed to a BLAKE3 Merkle ledger. Benchmarks demonstrate correctness across relativistic shocks, Kerr magnetospheres, and self-gravitating collapse.
\end{abstract}

